# XCU ctags
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# ctags run on small C sources; only the required objects (function
# definitions, type definitions, macros with arguments) and the main rule
# are required to appear, extra tags are tolerated. Tag lines are read back
# with grep and cut and the pattern is unescaped and checked against the
# defining line.

assertion  XCU.ctags.001
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#OUTPUT FILES
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD|SD
since      1992
says       Without -x a file named tags is written to the current directory;
           it has a name, file name and slash-delimited search pattern per
           line (tab separated), with lines for a function definition, a
           type definition and a macro with arguments, whose pattern is
           found in the defining line, and nothing for #if or #ifdef.
test       t/001-tags-file-format.sh

assertion  XCU.ctags.002
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#OUTPUT FILES
class      conditional
when       CD|SD
since      1992
says       The identifiers in the tags file are in ascending order of the
           collation sequence of the POSIX locale.
test       t/002-sorted.sh

assertion  XCU.ctags.003
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#EXTENDED DESCRIPTION
class      conditional
when       CD|SD
since      1992
says       The tag for main in a file is the file name with leading
           directories and the trailing .c removed, prefixed by M.
test       t/003-main-tag.sh

assertion  XCU.ctags.004
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       CD|SD
since      1992
says       -f writes the locators into the named file instead of tags, and
           -a adds to the existing file keeping its earlier lines.
test       t/004-file-and-append.sh

assertion  XCU.ctags.005
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#OPTIONS
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       CD|SD
since      1992
says       -x writes one line per object to standard output with the name,
           the line number, the file name and the text of that line
           separated by single spaces, and creates no tags file.
test       t/005-index-listing.sh

assertion  XCU.ctags.006
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#OPERANDS
class      conditional
when       CD|SD
since      1992
says       Files whose names end in .c or .h are scanned as C source, and
           several operands give tags from each file with its own name in
           the file column.
test       t/006-operands.sh

assertion  XCU.ctags.007
anchor     utilities/ctags.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       CD|SD
since      1992
says       A pathname operand that cannot be read gives a non-zero exit
           status.
test       t/007-missing-file.sh
